{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1208089-hope-in-the-darkness","id":1208089,"title":"Hope in the Darkness?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2018-04-17T11:44:43-07:00","id":1208089,"title":"Hope in the Darkness?","content":"So in the first Onyx Path podcast, the concept of hope was discussed in the context with the Chronicles of Darkness, with two games being described as the &quot;most hopeful&quot;- Promethean and Changeling. Now, Promethean is kind of obvious- it is a game about hope, becoming human and achieving New Dawn. Elpis is an actual force in that game, granting visions that while you are stuck in an eternal night right now, the sun would rise beyond the horizon, and that those who search would find. Changeling was described as having hope in an whole other type of context- that while you have been abused and mutilated beyond anything the human mind could tolerate, with a mind shattered and soul broken, you could still achieve Clarity and regain you life- or perhaps weave a new one. Your story hasn't ended- it has just began, and you are its writer. You are not a slave to the stories of the Fae, but you have regained control over your life, and now cement your own fate upon the story. Little Red Riding Hood is not devoured by the Wolf, waiting desperately to be saved by the Huntsmen. She cuts the Wolf's belly from the inside with a knife, cuts the Huntsmen head and go fourth to decide her own way to take.<br /> <br /> So yeah, both gamelines are clearly hopeful ones- but what about the others? I mean, the way I see it, there is no good horror story without having hope in it. If you know that all characters are doomed to die and have no way out, then there is no point in growing attached to them, and a story without relatable characters is, IMO, a story which should not be written :P There is always hope, as small and flitting as it may be- and in a dark world such as this, hope is the only thing which stops the whole complex of monsters and madmen from collapsing over their own heads.<br /> <br /> Hunter, for example, is truly an hopeful game in my eyes- it is the kind of hope that while fighting against all chances, you could actually succeed. It may be hard, it may require sacrifices, it may even kill you- but the Vigil would keeps on going, keep on protecting, keeps on holding the monsters in bay and show them that humanity can take a stand against the darkness and win. Sure, each candle is small, and each victory is meaningless on its own- but together, one by one, marching across the world and through the ages, the Vigil keeps on going. It is likely that the Vigil will never actually win, of course- but it would never lose either. It can't lose. If it would, well, that would be the end of humanity. The Vigil's fuel is hope- and without it, there will be no candle to light the darkness.<br /> <br /> Other gamelines also have their own hope- Demons hope to create their own Hell, and be free from the God Machine and its angelic servants. Mummies are slaves, but they have hope in achieving Apotheosis and reach the starry lands of A'aru, away from the tyranny of petty Laws and the hunger of the Devourer. Geist have hope, that you could look at the dissolution and madness brought by the Underworld and say &quot;no&quot;, helping ghosts to move on and, eventually, either free yourself from your burden or use them to change the very nature of the Great Bellow. Mage have hope that they could find escape from the Lie and reach the Truth once and for all. Beasts have hope that they could rise above the story they tell, freeing themselves from the terror of heroes and gather a family which they have chosen for themselves. Even Deviants may have hope, that they could get back at the organization which broken them and maintain their minds in the face of the Scars which were inflicted upon them.<br /> <br /> Among the gamelines, I think that Vampire and Werewolf are the least &quot;hopeful&quot;- Golconda is practically in the new edition, and as such there is no real &quot;escape from being a vampire&quot;, and Forsaken is a game of hunt, violence and death. Still, I think that there is some hope in Requiem- not a way out as much as having the ability to stay human even in the face of becoming a monster, and learning how to combine your own song and dance to those around you. Among all gamelines (other than Hunter), Vampire is the one in which you must maintain your memory of what being human actually is. You wear masks upon masks, lie to yourself and others, and in that mess of lies there is the hope that while you are a creature of the night, you could still remember the sun's loving embrace. Werewolf is a bit more problematic, but I think that its hope is that you are not bound to the influences of spirits and whispers of the shadows. That when things go bad, you could actually fight head to head against the forces of pain and sorrow, death and misfortune, and force them to obey instead of being bound to their will. And as you rise to become a Bodhisattva of the hunt, your pack would have to fear nothing- for there is nothing which could withstand your fangs or survive your claws, and only the fools would dare to threaten those dear to you.<br /> <br /> So- what do you think is the place of hope in the CofD?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-17T13:27:15-07:00","id":1208141,"title":"","content":"I think hope is the engine of action. <br /> <br /> However, hope consists of the joining of three elements: Goal, Ability and Agency.<br /> <br /> Goal is either an end-state or an intermediate step if the end is not reasonably foreseeable. It's the promise of a dollar more tomorrow than today that encourages working through the misery. It's lasting through the night one more time and being able to smile at yourself in the mirror and lie convincingly past the fangs that you're a good guy--still human.<br /> <br /> Ability is simply that you have resources, education or instruction, materials, funding, friends--whatever you need, to get the job done. If you clearly lack resources, your goal gets dragged down to more and more realistic levels of attainability until it reaches meager levels such as &quot;one foot forward... do it again&quot; or &quot;take a bite... chew.&quot; These can substitute for a time, but it takes indomitable will to avoid snapping after a while (see Holocaust and other total institutional survivors for examples, or medical suffering stories). <br /> <br /> Agency is whether others permit you to take action toward your goal. If you can reasonably expect your sandcastle to be stomped on as soon as you get a tower together, you will not bother to build it. Likewise, if you can only build it at the edge of the water, you may just wait until the tide is going <i>out</i> and not in.... As with resources, your goal gets dragged lower and lower until you arrive at a level that is attainable.<br /> <br /> Like any engine, momentum is important. If you have achieved a small hope, you can work toward a bigger one, and so on. Succeeding in tiny hopes build little momentum. Jumping immediately to goals that are too large--vastly exceeding your history of achievement, obviously out of line with resources or agency, or with serious consequences for failure--can undo momentum and destroy people in ways that even bullets don't.<br /> <br /> ---<br /> <br /> This framework can be helpful to think about while defining your characters as people, and conversely very handy to keep in mind as you consider how to defeat that semi-human monster who'd otherwise be unreachable through physical harm....<br /> <br /> --Khanwulf","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12493-khanwulf","name":"Khanwulf","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12493_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"898"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-17T13:42:15-07:00","id":1208153,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LostLight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1208089-hope-in-the-darkness#post1208089\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Werewolf is a bit more problematic, but I think that its hope is that you are not bound to the influences of spirits and whispers of the shadows. That when things go bad, you could actually fight head to head against the forces of pain and sorrow, death and misfortune, and force them to obey instead of being bound to their will. And as you rise to become a Bodhisattva of the hunt, your pack would have to fear nothing- for there is nothing which could withstand your fangs or survive your claws, and only the fools would dare to threaten those dear to you.<br /> <br /> So- what do you think is the place of hope in the CofD?</div> </div> </div> </div>I think the big hope for them is to become the new Father Wolf. It's even mentioned in the Storm Lord write-up. That's more of an end-game 'There can be only one' type of mindset, however, and is tied into the second one.<br /> <br /> Their land is gone, they're stuck traveling between two worlds that they don't belong to. Getting Pangaea back, a place where the sacred hunt rite isn't needed, where they fit and belong, where they don't have to rely on spirits to connect them, or humanity to anchor them, it's a pretty far-fetched hope but certainly one to aim for. It's linked to the heart of Father Wolf and his creation, so someone achieving that one may potentially achieve this.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 04-17-2018, 04:45 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-17T14:32:54-07:00","id":1208181,"title":"","content":"If yer gonna ask me, it's Vampire and Mummy that tie for most bleak. Mummy is it's own argument-is it better to be beautifully, nobly powerless or is it better to surrender to the blood and chains for the power to actually <i>do</i> something-but as Vampire is concerned, I kind of always find it hopeful that, while there is an inevitability all vampires will crash into given enough time-that time can be <i>really</i> far off, and even in that long slippery slide, you have the strange chance to make something precious, and even damn near eternal.<br /> <br /> But then again, hope for me is often simpler. Hope often just means being able to enjoy a hotdog on a warm summer night, even if you'll puke it up half an hour later.<br /> <br /> It's the little things.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-18T06:15:14-07:00","id":1208413,"title":"","content":"I find werewolf and beast to be the most interesting ones to find hope for. Both find hope in the same thing, effectively- family. When the world around you is garbage, full of violence and death, you still have your family. They may be just as effed up as you, but you have each other, and that's important.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8122-archonares","name":"ArchonAres","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"316"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-18T08:02:10-07:00","id":1208451,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> So yeah, both gamelines are clearly hopeful ones- but what about the others? I mean, the way I see it, there is no good horror story without having hope in it. If you know that all characters are doomed to die and have no way out, then there is no point in growing attached to them, and a story without relatable characters is, IMO, a story which should not be written :P </div> </div> </div>You're being too essentialist about it. As the audience it's quite possible to hope for an ending you intellectually know isn't possible. It's the basic idea behind tragedy.<br /> <br /> I'm not really sure how you would write a story without some kind of hope.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-18T08:10:47-07:00","id":1208455,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Michael</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1208089-hope-in-the-darkness?p=1208451#post1208451\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You're being too essentialist about it. As the audience it's quite possible to hope for an ending you intellectually know isn't possible. It's the basic idea behind tragedy.<br /> <br /> I'm not really sure how you would write a story without some kind of hope.</div> </div> </div> </div>I've never said that the hope has to be possible. Hope is defined by believing that you have a way out. The chances of that hope actually existing are irrelevant. What you need is the characters to believe- and as such, the audience to believe- that there is hope. Hope is the carrot dangled before the horse, as it was said :P<br /> <br /> And I have read my share of books and saw enough films which didn't had enough hope in them, if not one at all. That's why they sucked, IMO.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-18T08:25:26-07:00","id":1208456,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LostLight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1208089-hope-in-the-darkness?p=1208455#post1208455\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I've never said that the hope has to be possible. Hope is defined by believing that you have a way out. The chances of that hope actually existing are irrelevant. What you need is the characters to believe- and as such, the audience to believe- that there is hope. Hope is the carrot dangled before the horse, as it was said</div> </div> </div> </div>Actually, you did. That's literally what you said.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> If <b>you</b> know that all characters are doomed to die and have no way out, then there is no point in growing attached to them, </div> </div> </div>But yeah if you're saying that characters with no hope are boring... well yeah. That's a very low bar to set.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-18T08:35:30-07:00","id":1208460,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Michael</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1208089-hope-in-the-darkness?p=1208456#post1208456\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Actually, you did. That's literally what you said.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> But yeah if you're saying that characters with no hope are boring... well yeah. That's a very low bar to set.</div> </div> </div> </div>I stand behind what I said. If you know that there is no hope, and the writer made sure that you can't even imagine hope, or that the characters themselves can't see any hope to their situation, it is something I personally find really boring (and from my experience, more common than you think). I've seen what I consider to be good tragedy and horror and what I consider lousy tragedy and horror. I define hope as as an illusion in the first place, something which is not real yet makes you think it may be really, no matter how slim the chances are- so what I said was about knowing that all characters are going to die a terrible death and don't even have the illusion of escape is something I find as uninteresting. It may clarify a bit the meaning of my post- hope is not an happy ending, but easy it is to believe that such an happy ending is possible, no matter what reality has to say about it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-22T07:22:40-07:00","id":1210012,"title":"","content":"Funny thing is that I always thought of Changeling as being one of the bleakest games. I get the lens through which it can be hopeful, though.<br /> <br /> It may just be me, but I have long felt that CofD is a pretty hopeful series of games. Not that aweful things don't happen, but people endure and survive. They carve out their niches. They build their families. Chronicles is in many ways much more down to earth than your classics sword and sorcery RPG, so it's protagonists reflect the ways that real people deal with terrible shit without losing hope.<br /> <br /> Maybe that's because I'm a big softy who likes happy endings. Maybe it's because I was introduced to CofD by way of Promethean 1e. Maybe it's because I'm such an optimist that I can find a ray of hope in the grim darkness of 40k (it is there. The people who give a shit about each other, who care and love, who fight not for the God-Emperor but for their friends and loved ones.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://tinyurl.com/2p8ss75f\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Chris H</b></a>/<b>EndDaysEngine</b> | <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/EndDaysEngine\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Patreon</b></a></span>| <b>He/His </b>| <b>Currently Writing</b>: <i>[Redacted], [Redacted]</i><br /> <br /> <b>CofD booklists: </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/DRdB7h\" target=\"_blank\">Beast</a> I <a href=\"https://goo.gl/x1FPpM\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/ZSCx5U\" target=\"_blank\">Demon</a> | <a href=\"http://shorturl.at/syDK9\" target=\"_blank\">Deviant</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/Mh5M6m\" target=\"_blank\">Geist</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/gSjfm5\" target=\"_blank\">Hunter</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/qj5aX9\" target=\"_blank\">Mage</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/2HCpjg\" target=\"_blank\">Mummy</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/68yRHY\" target=\"_blank\">Promethean</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/a4mjqA\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/hrULtN\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf</a>","edited":{"userid":4433,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","user":"Second Chances","date":". 04-22-2018, 11:21 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","name":"Second Chances","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-22T19:28:51-07:00","id":1210234,"title":"","content":"I can't say whether it's true for everyone, but Requiem has always been the bleakest of all the lines I've played.<br /> <br /> From what I've read and played of Requiem, there really isn't a lot of hope for the Kindred at all beyond just dying again; you are a monstrous junkie, there's no getting better, and eventually everything you love will be dead, whether by time or your hand in case you frenzy.<br /> <br /> Then with the lack of Golconda being a thing anymore, and how the books focus on how being a vampire ruins the lives of everyone around you (based on reading half damned and the other books), I can't really easily associate hope with Requiem. It's certainly not as bleak as Masquerade was, but you're not even going to break even in Requiem from what I've experienced.<br /> <br /> Or it could be I'm a pessimist and I'm missing something. Could go either way, really.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12436-ever-professional","name":"Ever Professional","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12436_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"506"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-23T12:52:35-07:00","id":1210551,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1208089-hope-in-the-darkness?p=1208181#post1208181\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> But then again, hope for me is often simpler. Hope often just means being able to enjoy a hotdog on a warm summer night, even if you'll puke it up half an hour later.<br /> <br /> It's the little things.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is were I find myself too, more or less, because to me finding your own little place and being able to enjoy the little things at the end of an awful day is pretty much the kind of happiness I tend to consider important in horror settings, especially with monsters as main characters. I'm the kind of person who'd dedicate a story to a group of Prometheans who endure a lot to try to build a cool toy train and play with it, given the chance.<br /> <br /> But also because...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Second Chances</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1208089-hope-in-the-darkness?p=1210012#post1210012\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Maybe that's because I'm a big softy who likes happy endings. Maybe it's because I was introduced to CofD by way of Promethean 1e. Maybe it's because I'm such an optimist that I can find a ray of hope in the grim darkness of 40k (it is there. The people who give a shit about each other, who care and love, who fight not for the God-Emperor but for their friends and loved ones.)</div> </div> </div> </div>...I also agree with this. I think hope's important for the CofD and the games actually provide motivations and tools to aknowledge and support it. Bleak is good, horror is good, pain is good, but there's gotta be some light and hope there. Like in W40k or even Dark Souls and Berserk. Or Hellboy, which is my golden standard and keeps telling everyone that the world is doomed (and delivering that doom more and more), making its protagonists and readers suffer and yet still has its funny moments and leaves open a spot for a well earned, bittersweet ending.<br /> <br /> So I'm pretty much that. The more the odds are stacked against the protagonist, the more I enjoy rays of hope in my CofD gamelines.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/815620-cinder-s-comprehensive-collection-of-creations\" target=\"_blank\">Cinder's Comprehensive Collection of Creations</a> - Homebrew Hub<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1172470-cinder-writes-about-beast-the-primordial\" target=\"_blank\">I write about Beast: The Primordial a lot</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/38-cinder","name":"Cinder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar38_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1408"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-24T06:25:56-07:00","id":1210926,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ever Professional</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1208089-hope-in-the-darkness?p=1210234#post1210234\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I can't say whether it's true for everyone, but Requiem has always been the bleakest of all the lines I've played.<br /> <br /> From what I've read and played of Requiem, there really isn't a lot of hope for the Kindred at all beyond just dying again; you are a monstrous junkie, there's no getting better, and eventually everything you love will be dead, whether by time or your hand in case you frenzy.<br /> <br /> Then with the lack of Golconda being a thing anymore, and how the books focus on how being a vampire ruins the lives of everyone around you (based on reading half damned and the other books), I can't really easily associate hope with Requiem. It's certainly not as bleak as Masquerade was, but you're not even going to break even in Requiem from what I've experienced.<br /> <br /> Or it could be I'm a pessimist and I'm missing something. Could go either way, really.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> \u200bWell you're not wrong. But: as <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar4433_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"4433\" data-vbnamecard=\"4433\">Second Chances</a> points out for 40k, the hope in Requiem is generated by the characters who decide to go one more night in furtherance of something they care about. They create that care, or nurture it, and those are distinctly human things. It's when the hope fails completely, the ember dies out, that they slide fast into draugr and are lost. Even then, however, you could argue that there may--may--be means to bring them back from the abyss. <br /> <br /> But Requiem is really about the little hopes, the tiny things that keep you going even though you are a junkie and do do terrible things you'd rather not and struggle to resist. That struggle is a form of hope. Question is (rhetorical question), does it shine through in your game experience? Or does it get overshadowed by <i>blessed with suck</i>? In the end it's up to the table which story they enjoy.<br /> <br /> --Khanwulf","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12493-khanwulf","name":"Khanwulf","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12493_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"898"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-24T15:25:14-07:00","id":1211181,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Second Chances</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1208089-hope-in-the-darkness?p=1210012#post1210012\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Funny thing is that I always thought of Changeling as being one of the bleakest games. I get the lens through which it can be hopeful, though.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts, from a while back</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/805704-meet-the-huntsmen/page35\">-there, dressed in the blood of maggots with the dreaming toads and the sleeping snakes coiled around the singing mycelium, there, Lost is found in the simple promise that shatters worlds and breaks fates, there in the words &quot;<i>I am never going back</i>.&quot;</a></div> </div> </div> </div>I said some things on this, granted in an old context.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}